// the rest of the declaration file is deliberately absent.
//
// This file is ordinary vilan source, not a build artifact: review it, edit
// it, and commit it. Nothing regenerates it behind your back.
//
// `// TODO(bindgen)` marks a TypeScript construct the generator could not
// express in vilan. Nothing was dropped silently — every one is named.
//
// ONE rule is stated here rather than repeated everywhere: vilan has no
// `null`, and `Option<T>` cannot cross a host boundary — it is a tagged
// array (`Some(v)` is `[0, v]`, `None` is `[1]`) that a third-party host
// neither produces nor reads. So a TypeScript type admitting `null` or
// `undefined` binds as the BARE type, and the absence is yours to guard.
// Each such binding carries a `///` note saying so.

